(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the foundational structure of an HTML5 document, detailing each core tag from <!DOCTYPE html> to closing </html>.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   An HTML5 document is organized as a structured hierarchy of nested elements that browser) Tj
T*
(   rendering engines parse to construct the Document Object Model \(DOM\) tree:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. <!DOCTYPE html>: The document type declaration. In HTML5, it is simplified to a single clean) Tj
T*
(   line that signals to modern web browsers to render the document in standard mode rather than) Tj
T*
(   quirks mode.) Tj
T*
(   2. <html lang="en">: The root element encapsulating all page contents. The 'lang' attribute) Tj
T*
(   specifies the primary language, essential for search engine indexing and assistive screen) Tj
T*
(   readers.) Tj
T*
(   3. <head>: The metadata container containing non-visible configuration instructions:) Tj
T*
(   - <meta charset="UTF-8">: Declares Unicode character encoding to support all global scripts.) Tj
T*
(   - <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">: Sets responsive) Tj
T*
(   mobile viewport width and initial zoom scale.) Tj
T*
(   - <title>: Defines the document title displayed on browser tab bars and search engine results) Tj
T*
(   pages \(SERPs\).) Tj
T*
(   - <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">: Links external cascading style sheets.) Tj
T*
(   4. <body>: Encapsulates all visible document content rendered in the viewport, including text) Tj
T*
(   headings, paragraphs, images, tables, forms, and semantic layout sections.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Compare HTML4 block layout elements \(<div>, <span>\) with HTML5 semantic elements \(<header>, <nav>, <main>, <article>, <section>, <aside>, <footer>\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   HTML4 relied heavily on generic <div> \(block-level\) and <span> \(inline\) containers with class) Tj
T*
(   names \(e.g., <div class="header">\) to assemble page layouts. HTML5 introduced standardized) Tj
T*
(   Semantic Elements that fundamentally convey their structural role and meaning to browsers,) Tj
T*
(   search engine web crawlers, and assistive technologies:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. <header>: Introductory content or navigational aid for a page or section, containing) Tj
T*
(   branding, logos, or primary headings.) Tj
T*
(   2. <nav>: Designated section containing primary internal and external navigation hyperlinks.) Tj
T*
(   3. <main>: The central, unique content of the document, strictly appearing only once per) Tj
T*
(   document without repeating across pages.) Tj
T*
(   4. <article>: Self-contained, independently redistributable or syndicable content \(e.g., blog) Tj
T*
(   article, forum post, product card\).) Tj
T*
(   5. <section>: Thematic grouping of content, typically including an explicit heading \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   chapter, tabbed panel\).) Tj
T*
(   6. <aside>: Tangential content related indirectly to surrounding content \(sidebars, callout) Tj
T*
(   boxes, related links\).) Tj
T*
(   7. <footer>: Concluding footer content containing copyright notices, legal disclaimers, contact) Tj
T*
(   details, or sitemaps.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Benefits: Dramatically improves Search Engine Optimization \(SEO\), web accessibility for screen) Tj
T*
(   readers \(WAI-ARIA compliance\), and code maintainability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
