(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structure and implementation of HTML Tables, detailing <thead>, <tbody>, <tfoot>, colspan, rowspan, and accessibility captioning.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   HTML tables represent multidimensional structured data organized in horizontal rows and) Tj
T*
(   vertical columns:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Core Elements:) Tj
T*
(   1. <table>: Outer container defining the tabular grid.) Tj
T*
(   2. <caption>: Provides a descriptive title or accessibility summary for the table, placed) Tj
T*
(   immediately after <table>.) Tj
T*
(   3. <thead>: Groups the table header rows containing column headings. Contains <tr> and <th>) Tj
T*
(   elements.) Tj
T*
(   4. <tbody>: Groups the data-bearing body rows of the table. Contains <tr> and <td> elements.) Tj
T*
(   5. <tfoot>: Groups summary or total calculation rows at the base of the table.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Cell Merging Attributes:) Tj
T*
(   - colspan="n": Merges a cell horizontally across n contiguous columns.) Tj
T*
(   - rowspan="n": Merges a cell vertically down across n contiguous rows.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Accessibility Best Practices:) Tj
T*
(   Header cells \(<th>\) should include scope="col" \(for column headers\) or scope="row" \(for row) Tj
T*
(   headers\), enabling screen readers to announce corresponding labels when users navigate across) Tj
T*
(   individual data cells \(<td>\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the HTML Form architecture, explaining the <form> element attributes: action, method, enctype, and novalidate.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   An HTML form collects user inputs and transmits them to a web server for backend processing:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Form Attributes:) Tj
T*
(   1. action: Specifies the target URL or server endpoint \(e.g., '/api/login' or 'process.php'\)) Tj
T*
(   where form data is submitted. If omitted, the form submits to the current URL.) Tj
T*
(   2. method: Defines the HTTP request method used for submission:) Tj
T*
(   - GET: Appends form data key-value pairs as a query string in the URL \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   '?user=john&role=admin'\). Suitable for non-sensitive searches; data is bookmarkable and cached.) Tj
T*
(   - POST: Transmits form data inside the HTTP request body. Mandatory for sensitive data) Tj
T*
(   \(passwords\), large payloads, and state-modifying actions.) Tj
T*
(   3. enctype: Specifies the MIME encoding type of the submitted payload:) Tj
T*
(   - application/x-www-form-urlencoded \(Default\): Form values are URL-encoded.) Tj
T*
(   - multipart/form-data: Mandatory when uploading files \(<input type="file">\); packages payload) Tj
T*
(   as binary MIME parts.) Tj
T*
(   - text/plain: Sends plain unencoded text.) Tj
T*
(   4. novalidate: A boolean attribute instructing browsers to bypass native HTML5 validation) Tj
T*
(   constraints upon submission.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Categorize and explain the complete set of HTML5 Form Input Types with appropriate code examples and use cases.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   HTML5 expanded <input> types to provide native validation and mobile-optimized soft keyboards) Tj
T*
(   without external JavaScript:) Tj
T*
ET

