T*
(   HTML5 natively validates form inputs prior to dispatching HTTP requests to the backend server:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Validation Attributes:) Tj
T*
(   1. required: Halts submission and shows a browser tooltip if the field is empty.) Tj
T*
(   2. pattern="regex": Compares input against a regular expression pattern \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   pattern="[A-Z]{5}[0-9]{4}[A-Z]{1}" for PAN card numbers\).) Tj
T*
(   3. min and max: Enforces numerical bounds on number and date inputs.) Tj
T*
(   4. minlength and maxlength: Restricts string character count bounds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   JavaScript Custom Validation API:) Tj
T*
(   Form controls provide the ValidityState object accessed via element.validity \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   valueMissing, typeMismatch, patternMismatch, rangeOverflow, valid\). Developers can call) Tj
T*
(   element.setCustomValidity\("Custom error message"\) to inject tailored feedback, which blocks) Tj
T*
(   submission until cleared with an empty string.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
