(   2. Contrast with Traditional HTTP Cookies:) Tj
T*
(   - Size Limit: Cookies are restricted to 4KB per cookie; Web Storage allows 5-10MB.) Tj
T*
(   - Network Overhead: Cookies are automatically appended to the HTTP header of EVERY single) Tj
T*
(   request made to that domain, creating wasted bandwidth on static asset fetches. Web Storage) Tj
T*
(   data is purely client-side and never sent across the network.) Tj
T*
(   - Security: Cookies with HttpOnly flag prevent XSS theft. Web Storage is fully accessible to) Tj
T*
(   JavaScript, making it susceptible to XSS token theft.) Tj
