(   [Problem Statement]: Describe Responsive Web Design foundational HTML principles, including viewport configuration and the <picture> element.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Responsive web design ensures web layouts adapt dynamically across smartphones, tablets,) Tj
T*
(   laptops, and ultra-wide desktop monitors:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Viewport Meta Tag:) Tj
T*
(   `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">`) Tj
T*
(   - Instructs mobile browsers to set screen width to the physical device width rather than) Tj
T*
(   emulating a 980px desktop canvas, preventing tiny unreadable text and horizontal scrolling.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The <picture> Element and 'srcset':) Tj
T*
(   Enables Art Direction and bandwidth optimization by serving tailored image resolutions:) Tj
T*
(   ```html) Tj
T*
(   <picture>) Tj
T*
(   <source media="\(min-width: 1024px\)" srcset="banner-large.webp">) Tj
T*
(   <source media="\(min-width: 600px\)" srcset="banner-medium.webp">) Tj
T*
(   <img src="banner-small.webp" alt="Responsive Hero Banner">) Tj
T*
(   </picture>) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
(   The browser evaluates CSS media queries and downloads ONLY the optimal image asset, saving) Tj
T*
(   cellular data for mobile users.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
