(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Web Accessibility \(A11y\) standards, the WAI-ARIA framework, and HTML practices for screen reader compatibility.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Web Accessibility ensures web applications are fully usable by individuals with visual,) Tj
T*
(   auditory, motor, or cognitive disabilities:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Key Architectural Principles:) Tj
T*
(   1. Semantic HTML First: Always prioritize native semantic elements \(<button>, <nav>, <main>,) Tj
T*
(   <input>\) over styled <div> elements. Native elements have built-in keyboard navigation and) Tj
T*
(   screen reader roles.) Tj
T*
(   2. Descriptive Text Alternatives: Every <img> must supply an accurate alt attribute. For purely) Tj
T*
(   decorative graphics, use alt="" so screen readers skip them.) Tj
T*
(   3. Explicit Form Labeling: Pair every form input with a <label for="id"> so screen readers) Tj
T*
(   announce field names during tab navigation.) Tj
T*
(   4. WAI-ARIA \(Accessible Rich Internet Applications\):) Tj
T*
(   - Roles \(role="dialog", role="tablist"\): Exposes complex custom UI widgets to assistive) Tj
T*
(   technology.) Tj
T*
