(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the HTML5 Geolocation API, detailing permission flows, methods, and position data properties.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The HTML5 Geolocation API provides programmatic access to the user's geographical latitude and) Tj
T*
(   longitude coordinates:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Security & Permission Model:) Tj
T*
(   Because location is privacy-sensitive, the API functions strictly over secure HTTPS contexts.) Tj
T*
(   The browser automatically displays an interactive prompt asking the user for explicit) Tj
T*
(   permission. Access is rejected if denied.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Core API Methods:) Tj
T*
(   1. navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition\(successCallback, errorCallback, options\): Retrieves) Tj
T*
(   a one-time snapshot of the device's location.) Tj
T*
(   2. navigator.geolocation.watchPosition\(successCallback, errorCallback, options\): Registers a) Tj
T*
(   listener that fires repeatedly whenever device location changes \(for GPS tracking/navigation\).) Tj
T*
(   3. clearWatch\(watchId\): Cancels an active watchPosition listener.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Position Object Coordinates:) Tj
T*
(   The success callback receives a Position object containing coords.latitude, coords.longitude,) Tj
T*
(   coords.accuracy \(in meters\), coords.altitude, coords.heading, and coords.speed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
