(   [Problem Statement]: Explain HTML5 Drag and Drop API architecture, detailing events, dataTransfer object, and drag workflows.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   HTML5 introduced native desktop-style Drag and Drop \(DnD\) capabilities into browser web) Tj
T*
(   applications:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Making Elements Draggable:) Tj
T*
(   An element is designated as draggable by specifying draggable="true" \(e.g., `<div) Tj
T*
(   draggable="true">Drag me</div>`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Event Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   1. On Draggable Source: 'dragstart' \(initializes transfer payload\), 'drag' \(fires continuously) Tj
T*
(   during motion\), and 'dragend' \(cleans up after release\).) Tj
T*
(   2. On Drop Target: 'dragenter', 'dragover' \(must call event.preventDefault\(\) to permit) Tj
T*
(   dropping\), 'dragleave', and 'drop' \(processes the dropped payload\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The DataTransfer Object:) Tj
T*
(   Used to store and retrieve data exchanged between drag source and drop target:) Tj
T*
(   - event.dataTransfer.setData\("text/plain", data\): In dragstart, serializes payload.) Tj
T*
(   - event.dataTransfer.getData\("text/plain"\): In drop event, deserializes data.) Tj
T*
(   - event.dataTransfer.effectAllowed and dropEffect: Configures cursor feedback \(copy, move,) Tj
T*
(   link\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

