BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe HTML5 Web Workers, explaining why they are needed, how they communicate, and their technical limitations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   JavaScript in the browser runs in a single-threaded event loop. If a script executes an) Tj
T*
(   intensive mathematical calculation or image processing algorithm, the UI freezes, resulting in) Tj
T*
(   an unresponsive browser tab.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   HTML5 Web Workers Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Web Workers run JavaScript background threads in an isolated OS thread completely separate) Tj
T*
(   from the main execution thread.) Tj
T*
(   - Spawning a Worker: `const myWorker = new Worker\('worker.js'\);`) Tj
T*
(   - Communication via Message Passing:) Tj
T*
(   - Main thread posts data: `myWorker.postMessage\({data: heavyArray}\);`) Tj
T*
(   - Worker receives data: `onmessage = function\(e\) { /* compute */ postMessage\(result\); };`) Tj
T*
(   - Main thread receives result: `myWorker.onmessage = function\(e\) { updateUI\(e.data\); };`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Technical Limitations:) Tj
T*
(   Web Workers have NO access to the DOM, document, window, or parent page objects to prevent) Tj
T*
(   thread concurrency race conditions. However, they DO have access to navigator, location,) Tj
T*
(   XMLHttpRequest, Fetch API, and setTimeout.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 15:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the differences between asynchronous script loading mechanisms: default <script>, async, and defer.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   How JavaScript scripts are loaded and executed profoundly influences page rendering speed and) Tj
T*
(   Cumulative Layout Shift \(CLS\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Standard `<script src="app.js">`:) Tj
T*
(   - Parser-Blocking: HTML document parsing halts immediately when the tag is encountered. The) Tj
T*
(   browser downloads the script and executes it before parsing resumes.) Tj
T*
(   - Placing scripts in `<head>` blocks rendering, leading to blank screens.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. `<script async src="app.js">`:) Tj
T*
(   - Asynchronous Download: Downloaded in parallel with HTML parsing without blocking.) Tj
T*
(   - Immediate Execution: As soon as download completes, HTML parsing pauses while the script) Tj
T*
(   executes immediately.) Tj
T*
(   - Execution Order NOT Guaranteed: Scripts execute in order of download completion. Ideal for) Tj
T*
(   independent third-party trackers and analytics \(e.g., Google Analytics\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. `<script defer src="app.js">`:) Tj
T*
(   - Deferred Execution: Downloaded in parallel during HTML parsing.) Tj
T*
(   - Executes strictly AFTER HTML parsing is 100% complete, just before DOMContentLoaded fires.) Tj
T*
(   - Execution Order GUARANTEED: Multiple deferred scripts execute in the exact order they appear) Tj
T*
(   in markup. Ideal for application scripts that depend on DOM elements or other scripts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 16:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
