(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the security implications of iframe embedding, explaining clickjacking attacks and the 'sandbox' attribute.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The <iframe> element embeds external web pages within a parent document, introducing critical) Tj
T*
(   security vectors:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Clickjacking Attack:) Tj
T*
(   An attacker overlays a transparent, invisible iframe of a legitimate banking or social media) Tj
T*
(   site over an enticing decoy button \('Click here to win a car!'\). When the user clicks, they) Tj
T*
(   unknowingly submit transactions on the embedded site. Defended by sending the `X-Frame-Options:) Tj
T*
(   DENY` HTTP header or `Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The 'sandbox' Attribute:) Tj
