(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the HTML5 History API and how it enables Single Page Applications \(SPAs\) without full page reloads.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   In traditional web applications, navigating to a new URL triggers a full browser reload. Single) Tj
T*
(   Page Applications \(SPAs\) utilize the HTML5 History API to update the browser address bar) Tj
T*
(   dynamically while updating the view via JavaScript:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Key Methods:) Tj
T*
(   1. history.pushState\(stateObject, title, url\): Adds a new URL entry to the browser session) Tj
T*
(   history stack without initiating an HTTP page fetch or reload.) Tj
T*
(   2. history.replaceState\(stateObject, title, url\): Modifies the current history entry without) Tj
T*
(   pushing a new record.) Tj
T*
(   3. window.onpopstate Event: Listens for user navigation clicks on the browser Back or Forward) Tj
T*
(   buttons, allowing the client router to render the corresponding page view seamlessly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
