BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze common HTML parsing pitfalls, Quirks Mode vs Standards Mode, and DOM tree construction rules.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Browser HTML parsers operate under complex legacy compatibility rules:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Standards Mode vs Quirks Mode:) Tj
T*
(   - Standards Mode: Triggered by a valid `<!DOCTYPE html>`. The browser parses markup according) Tj
T*
(   to strict W3C/WHATWG specifications.) Tj
T*
(   - Quirks Mode: Triggered if <!DOCTYPE> is omitted or preceded by comments/text. The browser) Tj
T*
(   emulates archaic 1990s Netscape 4 / IE 5 layout bugs \(e.g., incorrect box model calculation) Tj
T*
(   where width includes padding and border\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. DOM Construction & Error Recovery:) Tj
T*
(   - The HTML parser never throws fatal syntax errors; it automatically corrects unclosed tags) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., unclosed `<p>` automatically closed when a block `<div>` appears\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mis-nested tags like `<b><i>text</b></i>` are reordered into valid tree nodes) Tj
T*
(   `<b><i>text</i></b><i></i>` by adoption agency algorithms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
